# .socraticodeignore — semantic-index exclusions (gitignore syntax).
# Layered on SocratiCode's built-in defaults + .gitignore.
#
# Vendored skill trees (managing-skills submodules) are not this project's
# code: they inflate embedding time and outrank first-party code in
# codebase_search results. See GH #182 / gregoryfoster/skills#76.
#
# NOTE: `skills/` is deliberately NOT excluded — this repo authors
# first-party skills there (brainstorming/, train-model/, writing-plans/)
# alongside symlinks into skills-vendor/. The indexer does not follow
# symlinks, so excluding skills-vendor/ already drops the vendored content.
#
# `.skills/` holds the vendored copy of managing-skills' doctor.sh — same
# class of content, kept out for the same reason.
skills-vendor/
.claude/skills/
.skills/

# `docs/plans/` is dated design prose — AGENTS.md: "dated snapshots, never
# current guidance". It was 981 chunks, 36.6% of the code index and 2.3x all
# of src/, and it outranked first-party source on questions the plans answer
# wrongly: a context search for the validated_addresses status CHECK returned
# a plan showing 'assigned', a value migration 014 dropped and that
# SENSITIVE-AREAS.md calls a derived rollup, never a stored status.
#
# Same argument as skills-vendor/ above, applied to our own prose — which is
# worse, because ours is more plausible. Excluded from the CODE index only:
# the identical content stays embedded as the `design-plans` context
# artifact, so plan rationale is still searchable via codebase_context_search
# (deliberate call) rather than surfacing unbidden in codebase_search.
# See GH #218 (option A); the context-store share is still open there.
docs/plans/
